From ec3803a49ef0ba3f4353bfcabca6a4c5e8c3c48a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:00:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.5.6: rmcpd get_wireless_stations curated read tool

Adds a BASE-tier read-only MCP tool exposing per-STA wireless link
detail: for every wl BSS the kernel exposes, list associated stations
with full `wl sta_info` (power-save state, negotiated bandwidth, tx/rx
rate, retries, rssi), plus per-radio `chanim_stats` channel health and
the live chanspec.

Takes NO caller-supplied input: the interface list comes from
/sys/class/net and STA MACs come from `assoclist`, so the fixed popen
pipeline carries no injection surface (same model as tool_firewall).
Output is raw `wl` text returned verbatim; it carries MACs/rates/rssi
only, never a PSK. MCP-only, so it is automatically absent from the
noMCP variant.

Built and metal-passed on RT-BE96U 2026-07-15: flashed, armed with diag
consent, connected over MCP from LAN; tools/list returns 10 base + 4
diag, all real data. Image sha 44c1bf65, loader ab3dbd9a.

This tool produced the per-STA data that exonerated the 6 GHz radio
under load (PS off, 320 MHz, EHT-MCS9, 3.6-4.3 Gbps PHY held across a
sustained download) and is the instrument for the ongoing 6 GHz
sawtooth investigation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
